     'The new dimensions must multiply to the original element count. A single -1 asks PyTorch to infer the missing size from that count; it does not mean reverse the axis.',
     '[1,2,3,4,5,6] reshaped into two rows becomes [[1,2,3],[4,5,6]]. Reading the result row by row recovers the original order.',
